  {
   "type": "Feature",
   "properties": {
    "name": "South Mountains (Dobbins Lookout)",
    "category": "metamorphic core complex",
    "rock_units": "West: Estrella Gneiss, Komatke Granite. East: South Mountains Granodiorite, Telegraph Pass Granite, Dobbins Alaskite (mylonitized)",
    "age": "Proterozoic basement; mid-Tertiary plutons; mylonitization ~21.6-19.4 Ma",
    "description": "A classic metamorphic core complex. Mid-Tertiary plutons were sheared beneath a low-angle detachment fault as the crust extended.",
    "sources": [
     {
      "title": "Reynolds 1985, Geology of the South Mountains, central Arizona (AZGS Bulletin 195)",
      "url": "https://azgs.arizona.edu/geologic-map-south-mountains-central-arizona"
